KG42.register("clusters-528518198e756328d9c9f32b",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v142-d-K002","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","label":"SDR net energy submission, conditional update control, and iterative pricing feedback","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"SDR net energy submission, conditional update control, and iterative pricing feedback","market_meaning":"Participants submit net energy profiles, and the coordinator receives supply and demand information and generates internal prices based on SDR; price feedback guides demand adjustments in the next round. When step-size control is adopted, bid updates are restricted, and the process stops according to the simulation convergence criterion or the iteration limit to establish a trading state. The current mathematical boundaries and some interfaces have not yet been closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The baseline response to current prices, optional control of the number of bids, relative change limits, and combined control each retain their adoption conditions. The GB day-ahead simulation and the Appendix B example are not generalized; the absolute power limits in the appendix are not equivalent to the relative change limits represented by rmp. The learning process is not replaced by the current-price chain, and physical network issues remain outside the coordinator's modeling scope.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is defined by the information dependencies through which bids form prices and prices feed back into bids, spanning submission, coordination, and pricing functions; post-termination trading arrangements and settlement-state selection reference this cluster's interfaces in K003.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides demand submission, conditional update restrictions, a price-response example, and an interface for terminating demand iteration."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Complements the supply side of net energy submission and the conditional application of the same control scheme to supply bids."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Connects the two types of net energy submission with the coordinator's receiving responsibility and retains the scope of the platform, metering, and intervention."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the iterative price-feedback process and its stopping conditions without equating stopping with proof of economic equilibrium."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Converts the received signed bids and external prices into SDR internal buying and selling prices."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04"],"rationale":"The source specifies optional freezing and change limits for participants' energy bids, and the two chains are complementary applications to demand and supply; bid variables and constraints with different sign ranges remain independent."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"rationale":"The A18 profile submitted to the coordinator in each round corresponds to demand submission and receipt when it takes nonnegative values in the relevant time periods; this is an assembly relationship between the two ends of the same submission activity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"rationale":"The negative components of the A18 profile correspond to supply submission and receipt by the coordinator. The expression in R003 may be read in conjunction with this relationship, but it does not backfill objects that have not been formalized in R002."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta-e-bid-SDR","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"rationale":"The source explicitly states that SDR is calculated from the received bids of all participants; submitted profiles become inputs in the pricing chain and must correspond to the same region, time period, and received round. No new scientific edge across chains is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C008"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::var_internal_price","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g07-ev-05","v141-b-g07-ev-11"],"rationale":"The internal buying and selling prices generated and published by the coordinator enter the iterative price signal; R008 declares no price variable objects, so only the expression outputs and existing variables in R004 are linked, without fabricating mappings of quantity objects."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g07-ev-14","v141-b-g07-ev-15"],"rationale":"Current internal prices drive individual decisions, and Appendix B specifically demonstrates demand rearrangement and resubmission; this feedback supports assembly without generalizing the example's convergence result into a general guarantee."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-I-max"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R004::theta::param_max_iterations"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"Stopping the demand process and stopping price coordination express the same last line of defense on the two process sides; joint termination does not mean that bids and prices have converged."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"rationale":"The same SDR demand-submission function appears in submission, receipt, and pricing inputs; the representative item is used only for display, and all related constraints and edges are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"rationale":"The nodes at all three locations carry the supply-submission function for SDR negative net energy bids; display normalization does not merge distinct constraints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"rationale":"Within the same mechanism, the coordinator receiving bids, executing the adopted update rules, and calculating prices is the same; a shared responsible entity is not in itself a basis for forming a cluster."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g07-ev-05","v141-b-g07-ev-14"],"rationale":"These nodes all refer to the SDR internal-price function; price generation, feedback, and use in the example still retain their respective conditions."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-rmp","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-rmp"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E14"],"rationale":"Within a single implementation adopting a uniform relative change-limit rule, both refer to rmp in Formula (8); their local parameter roles for demand and supply are retained, without presuming identical values across different cases."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-rmp-prime","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-rmp-prime"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03"],"rationale":"Both derive from rmp′ in the same combined-control example and are conditionally linked, but they are neither merged with ordinary rmp nor used to replace the missing correspondence between the proportion and set size."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-I-max","v141-c-R004::theta::param_max_iterations"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"Although the local notation differs, both refer to the preset iteration limit used as this paper's last line of defense; their demand-side and coordination-side roles are retained, and the case value of 200 is not made universal."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"All connections and object correspondences are established solely from unreviewed candidate evidence permitted in the experiment; the B transcriptions, C2 content, and this cluster have undergone neither independent source review nor scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-EV08","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05","v141-b-g07-ev-11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently check the relevant source text and formulas, then examine the conditional interfaces proposed here; retain the unverified status until verification."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"A21 in R008 does not specify how to handle zero aggregate demand; A19 also lacks price-domain conditions ensuring that its denominator is nonzero. The export price being lower than the retail price alone is insufficient to cover all algebraic inputs.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Obtain additional source explanations for zero demand, empty supply and demand sets, and the applicable domain of external prices; do not introduce an infinite SDR or substitute prices before these boundaries are clarified upstream."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R001-C001 uses a necessary-and-sufficient acceptance criterion, whereas the source explicitly states only that rejection is mandatory when the change limit is exceeded; the criterion also incorporates upper and lower bid bounds. It cannot be treated as the same constraint as R001-C005 merely because they share change-limit content.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Use subsequent B/C revisions to check the rejection obligation, other admission conditions, and acceptance timing, and clarify whether the source supports necessity and sufficiency; retain the frozen expression unchanged in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"A complete parameter correspondence has not yet been established between the rmp′ example in R001-C006 and the general combined-control expression in R002-C005; the latter expression uses rmp and a set prohibited from updating, which does not justify asserting that the two chains describe exactly the same numerical configuration.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-forbid-size","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-rmp-prime"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g02-e24"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop05","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Clarify the correspondence among the proportion permitted to update, the set size, and the two change-limit parameters in the combined-control example, and retain the difference in applicability between general control and the specific example; the related node proposals remain pending review."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G05","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The maximum price difference in R004 does not specify which time periods and buying and selling prices it ranges over; the price-change stopping condition does not simultaneously test for a bid fixed point and cannot establish that all bids converge or that a Nash equilibrium exists and has been found.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::var_internal_price","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::theta::param_convergence_tolerance"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-EV08","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g03-E16"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g04-EXT01"],"required_work":"Check the price-comparison set, iteration indices, and method for checking bid convergence, and distinguish numerical stopping from the determination of equilibrium; assembly must not introduce new convergence constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G06","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R003 retains the A18 expression but has no typed objects for its device quantities, while R002 references A18 only procedurally; the complete individual scheduling model has also not become a chain in this catalog. Therefore, the current connections cannot establish closure for device feasibility or the correspondence of bids to time periods and rounds.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R008::theta::theta-e-bid-SDR"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-01","v141-b-g07-ev-03"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g06-P01"],"required_work":"Clarify upstream the indices within the same mechanism, units, and object assignments for individual scheduling, submitted profiles, and pricing inputs; retain only the reference interfaces until the scheduling node proposal is approved."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G07","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The optional price bids in the general pricing function, the implementation model, and the absolute power limits in Appendix B have no approved independent nodes. Existing quantity-bid nodes do not thereby become price-bid nodes, nor are absolute power limits identified with relative change limits.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R008::theta::theta-p-bid","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g07-ev-11","v141-b-g08-e12"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p01","v141-b-g02-prop03","v141-b-g02-prop04","v141-b-g08-p01"],"required_work":"Manually examine the necessity and boundaries of these proposals individually; if the catalog is subsequently expanded, objects supported by sources should be added upstream. No nodes are approved or inserted in this round."}]},"rule_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R001","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R002","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R004","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","KG31-8571e493b8ecf84a","KG31-a9bd9e360b96ff06","KG31-e3df7b859b17cba0"]});
